\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O God, our help in ages past,
\par Our hope for years to come,
\par Our shelter from the stormy blast,
\par And our eternal home:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Under the shadow of Thy throne
\par Thy saints have dwelt secure;
\par Sufficient is Thine arm alone,
\par And our defence is sure.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Before the hills in order stood,
\par Or earth received her frame,
\par From everlasting Thou art God,
\par To endless years the same.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. A thousand ages in Thy sight
\par Are like an evening gone;
\par Short as the watch that ends the night
\par Before the rising sun.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The busy tribes of flesh and blood,
\par With all their cares and fears,
\par Are carried downward by the flood,
\par And lost in following years.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Time, like an ever-rolling stream,
\par Bears all its sons away;
\par They fly forgotten, as a dream
\par Dies at the opening day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. O God, our help in ages past,
\par Our hope for years to come,
\par Be Thou our guard while troubles last,
\par And our eternal home.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

